## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
- Minutes 10:30–10:54 (part 1): continuously heavy mixed traffic.
- Minutes 25–49 (part 2): severe congestion, near-standstill gridlock throughout; 4–10 auto-rickshaws per clip; Nirma University bus stationary in foreground minutes 25–27.
- Minutes 50–54: continuous heavy, largely gridlocked traffic.
- Minute 56 onward: congestion eased to flowing traffic toward the camera.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
- Pedestrians walking/crossing within the live carriageway and between queued vehicles: minutes 0, 12, 21, 25, 29, 36, 40, 41, 47, 49, 50, 56, 57, 58, 59.
- Motorcyclists/scooter riders filtering between lanes throughout, particularly during the gridlock of minutes 25–49 and 50–55.
- No wrong-way driving, helmetless riders or red-light jumping were specifically observed.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The junction was under continuous heavy load for the full hour. The first 25 minutes showed heavy but moving mixed traffic with a steady stream of identified vehicles; minutes 25–49 were the worst period, with near-standstill gridlock, stationary buses and trucks, and pedestrians and two-wheelers exploiting the queues to move through or between vehicles. Minutes 50–54 remained gridlocked before traffic began flowing toward the camera from minute 56. Dominant traffic was private cars (white/silver/grey/black) with a constant presence of yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws and dense two-wheeler filtering. Recurring elements: red city buses, goods/canvas trucks, tractors with tanker trailers (minutes 12 and 42), pedestrians habitually crossing between vehicles rather than at designated points, and emergency/police vehicles (ambulances minutes 0 and 58; police vehicles minutes 49 and 59).

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. Traffic was heavy or gridlocked for the entire 60-minute period; the closest to easing was the flowing traffic from minute 56 onward, which still carried dense mixed traffic.
