# CCTV REVIEW SUMMARY — cam14_stream-14 (Unknown Location, cam14)
**Footage:** 720 minutes (minutes 0–719), from approx. 21:23 Saturday 13-06-2026 to approx. 08:13 Sunday 14-06-2026. No alerts raised by the system at any point.

---

## 1. SCENE
The camera overlooks a large, signalised urban road junction with multiple approaches, zebra crossings, a central island, right-footpath shops (a "WESTBANK" sign visible at minutes 111, 114, 121, 150–174) and a bus shelter/hoarding on the right. The camera carries a "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" red-light-violation detection overlay, visible at minutes 124, 301, 309, 310, 313–316, 321, 477–482, 495, 497 and 650–699. The footage begins at night (approx. 21:23), runs through the small hours, pre-dawn and dawn, and ends in hazy/overcast morning light (approx. 08:13). Road surface was repeatedly wet/reflective, indicating recent rain or drizzle throughout the period (e.g. minutes 15, 21, 23, 29–32, 50–51, 58, 67, 77, 81, 84, 92, 96, 106, 109, 112, 118, 120, 252, 255–256, 261, 267–269, 271, 274, 281 onward, 303, 307, 313, 316, 318, 376, 387, 395–399, 435, 439, 449, 600–624).

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE
Traffic was continuous and mixed throughout. Dominant vehicle types:
- **Motorcycles/scooters** — the most numerous class throughout, roughly 6–25 per minute at night, 8–20 per minute in the morning; many carried pillion passengers (occasionally three riders, minute 281); riders in white, red, dark, orange, blue, yellow and light clothing; many appeared helmetless (minutes 210, 220, 224, 316, 575–599, 633).
- **Auto-rickshaws** — yellow-and-green (CNG) dominant, plus white, green, blue, red, black, yellow, yellow-blue and yellow-purple examples; typically 2–15 per minute; goods three-wheeler carriers in green/blue also seen (e.g. minutes 575, 581, 591, 595, 598, 650, 654, 658, 659, 664, 670, 687, 695).
- **Cars** — overwhelmingly white (hatchbacks, sedans, SUVs, MPVs, vans), plus dark/black, silver/grey, red, maroon, blue, gold/tan and one lime-green car (minute 618/219). A recurring white hatchback entered from the left and exited right around the 30s mark in nearly every minute from minute 2 to roughly minute 148.
- **Buses** — red/orange city buses (most frequent), blue-and-white city buses (DTC-style at minute 674), white coaches, double-deckers (red at 586, 639, 672–673; cream "JALARAM" at 578), GSRTC-identified bus (minute 36), "PUNJAB" livery coach (605), "DELHI" coach (639), "SALUJA BUS SERVICE" (582), "GURUDEV TRAVELS"/"GUILDFORD TRAVELS" (684), "JAMIA" (363), "401 Chandni" (620), "TANNA"/"ANNA" (616), "AMER" LED rear (287), "ANC" tarpaulin bus (183).
- **Goods vehicles/trucks** — box trucks, tippers, concrete mixers, tarpaulin-covered trucks, tankers (Bharat Petroleum-type, 637/644), container trucks ("BALA JI ...JAIPUR", 626; "R.K.M. LOGISTICS", 647), municipal tipper "AMC 15" (631), refuse trucks, road-roller (581), tractor-trolley (710), backhoe loaders (319, 483–487, 556, 558).
- **Emergency/official vehicles** — white SUV with blue beacon (175), ambulance-type vans with blue beacons (183, 188, 195), police vehicle with flashing lights (206), fire tender (269), ambulance-type vans (274, 277, 377, 382, 505, 480, 483), police SUV with light bar (631), beacons at 350–351, 462, 463, 466.
- **Pedestrians** — sparse overnight; crowds of ~20–50 gathered on the right footpath near the lit shops during the later night (parts 8–10, e.g. ~20–30 at minute 235); individual and small-group crossings throughout; cyclists intermittently (207, 209, 212–213, 365, 371, 538, 549, 557, 568, 571, 580, 583–584, 587, 590, 592, 625, 629, 636–637, 644, 646, 653, 656, 658, 668). Dogs on the carriageway at minutes 358, 466, 536, 592, 611, 614.

